{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1504048-complete-beast-newb-creation-help","id":1504048,"title":"Complete Beast Newb Creation Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-28T08:33:44-08:00","id":1504048,"title":"Complete Beast Newb Creation Help","content":"Hello, thank you in advance for being patient with me. I have been aplayer in a few other COD 2nd edition chronicles, but never a Beast before. I have the Beast core book and the players guide. So the chronicle we all started mortal - So I am going Beast - the other three players sounds like are going Werewolf, Mage, and Promethean.<br /> <br /> I went in as a very brawl physical character with some animal ken in birds. Going into the Chronicle we didn't know which Splat we were playing so it is hard to minmax. My Intelligence is 1, Manipulation is 1, and my Presence is 2. I mostly looking at Eshmaki and going for Hunger for Ruin - Beast Concept was a Dragon that likes to burn things / people that are important to people in order to teach lessons.<br /> <br /> 1) So looks like with Nightmares I will suck since most of the dicepools are Intelligence, Manipulation, and Presence. My Wits is 3 so I did see those two Nightmares - You Will Never Rest (Wits), You Cannot Run (Wits), but those two were the only Wits ones I can find. Short of raising my stats, am I just screwed on Nightmares? <br /> <br /> 2) For Atavisms I was looking to start with Dragonfire and Unbreakable as my Beast concept is essentially a Dragon. For Eshmaki Limb from Limb and Relentless Hunter also look good. Non-Family Atavisms I liked Wings of the Raptor and Titanic Blow. Anything else I should be considering?<br /> <br /> 3) Does the armor from Unbreakable stack with Advanced Ironskin or just normally wearing body armor (or anything else)?<br /> <br /> 4) For other merits I liked Killer Instinct (which I have all prereqs for), maybe Advanced Fast Reflexes and Hunger Management.<br /> <br /> 5) For Lair I was going with major - Burning and minor - Blazing Lights to start with. Any other suggestions on Lair?<br /> <br /> 6) Within having a high Strength and Brawl, anything else I should consider when making my character? Any other just general suggestions?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you in advance for your help!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27665-variable","name":"Variable","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27665_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T09:47:14-08:00","id":1504054,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Variable;n1504048My Intelligence is 1, Manipulation is 1, and my Presence is 2.[/quote]<br /> <br /> While not really something you can change now... in general for CofD games, I'd really advise against having two 1s in Attributes unless it's really vital to the concept. The CofD doesn't really like &quot;dump stats&quot; so a 1 in an Attribute is very likely to bite you in the ass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) So looks like with Nightmares I will suck since most of the dicepools are Intelligence, Manipulation, and Presence. My Wits is 3 so I did see those two Nightmares - You Will Never Rest (Wits), You Cannot Run (Wits), but those two were the only Wits ones I can find. Short of raising my stats, am I just screwed on Nightmares? </div> </div> </div>You're going to suck with Nightmares if you try to use them on other supernaturals. Against mortals, this is going to be a matter of Satiety management. Nightmares are strongest when you're at Satiety 7+, and most activation dice pools are either Attribute + Satiety vs. Attribute + Supernatural Tolerance, or Attribute + Satiety - Attribute. So if you're building up to Satiety 7 before you start hitting people with Nightmares, you're looking at 7-8 dice. Normal humans don't get a Supernatural Tolerance score, so the strongest opposition is either vs 5 dice or taking a -5 dice penalty. Not great, but functional, plus the high Satiety automatic bonus effect will be there too.<br /> <br /> There are also some Nightmares that don't roll, so you can look at those as options too.<br /> <br /> You also don't have to worry about being good at Nightmares. It's hard to make a Beast that's good at everything Beasts can do. Begotten that get into a lot of physical conflicts are better served by Atavisms which are stronger at low Satiety. Especially at start, it seems like you'll be better set learning how to manage Satiety to make best use of your Atavisms without running yourself to zero if you can avoid it, and then you can look at getting better at Nightmares later if you even feel like it (if your mage goes Mastigos... you can probably skip it).<br /> <br /> So, basically, don't worry too much about it. It's not your PC's strong suit, there's plenty to be good at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) For Atavisms I was looking to start with Dragonfire and Unbreakable as my Beast concept is essentially a Dragon. For Eshmaki Limb from Limb and Relentless Hunter also look good. Non-Family Atavisms I liked Wings of the Raptor and Titanic Blow. Anything else I should be considering? </div> </div> </div>Unless you're allowed to pick alternate Birthrights (those are in the Player's Guide, though you're not going to get much out of the Manipulation based one for Eshmaki), keep in mind that one of your big advantages is opening a fight with an unexpected/surprise attack. From the Shadows might not really fit the dragon theme as much as possible, combo it with the Eshmaki Birthright, Limb from Limb, and a targeted shot on a surprise attack (even easier with Advanced Killer Instinct), and you can inflict three Tilts on a target before the fight really starts.<br /> <br /> If you invest in Intimidate a bit, Looming Presence can make up for your low Presence rating if you want to play the &quot;heel&quot; of the group in social situations, and it's one of the best defensive Atavisms at the same time. This is a great way to end fights with your first hit, and have back up if it doesn't work. Terror's Friend is a good follow up pick on this as well.<br /> <br /> Shadowed Soul is another good addition to your stealth package for making sure you get into unexpected positions before your big opening attack.<br /> <br /> Smashing Currents and Lightning Strike are both strong picks for any close-combat Beast.<br /> <br /> Weakness Exposed is something to keep in mind, but you'll want it for later really. Killer Instinct is better in the immediate term, but eventually Weakness Exposed will be very useful for helping to deal with your low Attributes and ensure you're not left out of a bunch of situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Does the armor from Unbreakable stack with Advanced Ironskin or just normally wearing body armor (or anything else)? </div> </div> </div>Officially? Talk to your ST. Semi-officially, the CofD 2e advises that stacking is acceptable as long as it comes from different sources (or explicitly said to stack). But that still ends up with judgment calls. Two different sets of armor can't stack (not even if one was created with magic). Two armor granting Atavisms can't stack. Two armor granting Merits can't stack. Can a Merit that only Beasts can take stack with an Atavaism... maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) For other merits I liked Killer Instinct (which I have all prereqs for), maybe Advanced Fast Reflexes and Hunger Management. </div> </div> </div>Hunger Management is only really useful if you want to move around the Satiety track a lot (such as going high for using Nightmares, and then low for Atavisms). If you start focused on Atavisms you really aren't going to need this at start. Still useful for later though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) For Lair I was going with major - Burning and minor - Blazing Lights to start with. Any other suggestions on Lair? </div> </div> </div>This is a place where being thematic is best. Think about your Legend and make sure your Lair can build towards it. Potentially think about what kind of real world location suit you Legend and Lair so you can find new Chambers more effectively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) Within having a high Strength and Brawl, anything else I should consider when making my character? Any other just general suggestions? </div> </div> </div>Unless you take an Atavism or Merit to help with your damage type and/or output, Brawl tends to favor grappling. Fortunately, you have a lot of access to making your fists better weapons than anything people can make to swing around in their hands though. You're also going to want to make sure speed (both physical and mental) and movement are advantages you keep. It doesn't matter if you can rip a tank apart with your bare hands if you can't get to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T10:10:41-08:00","id":1504056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Variable</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1504048-complete-beast-newb-creation-help#post1504048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, thank you in advance for being patient with me. I have been aplayer in a few other COD 2nd edition chronicles, but never a Beast before. I have the Beast core book and the players guide. So the chronicle we all started mortal - So I am going Beast - the other three players sounds like are going Werewolf, Mage, and Promethean.<br /> <br /> I went in as a very brawl physical character with some animal ken in birds. Going into the Chronicle we didn't know which Splat we were playing so it is hard to minmax. My Intelligence is 1, Manipulation is 1, and my Presence is 2. I mostly looking at Eshmaki and going for Hunger for Ruin - Beast Concept was a Dragon that likes to burn things / people that are important to people in order to teach lessons.<br /> <br /> 1) So looks like with Nightmares I will suck since most of the dicepools are Intelligence, Manipulation, and Presence. My Wits is 3 so I did see those two Nightmares - You Will Never Rest (Wits), You Cannot Run (Wits), but those two were the only Wits ones I can find. Short of raising my stats, am I just screwed on Nightmares?<br /> 2) For Atavisms I was looking to start with Dragonfire and Unbreakable as my Beast concept is essentially a Dragon. For Eshmaki Limb from Limb and Relentless Hunter also look good. Non-Family Atavisms I liked Wings of the Raptor and Titanic Blow. Anything else I should be considering?<br /> 3) Does the armor from Unbreakable stack with Advanced Ironskin or just normally wearing body armor (or anything else)?<br /> 4) For other merits I liked Killer Instinct (which I have all prereqs for), maybe Advanced Fast Reflexes and Hunger Management.<br /> 5) For Lair I was going with major - Burning and minor - Blazing Lights to start with. Any other suggestions on Lair?<br /> 6) Within having a high Strength and Brawl, anything else I should consider when making my character? Any other just general suggestions?<br /> Thank you in advance for your help!</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, I would endorse you to not think of it as teaching lessons more of what your character stands for. I know the book encourages the former, the latter's going to do more for you.<br /> <br /> 1) I mean, as a brawl heavy, physical heavy character, the power type that relies more on subtlety and application of the Primordial Dream over the Horror is not gonna be your best. That said, Nightmares being keyed to Satiety means that you're going to have time after major feasts, you're going to be good at Nightmares-which is by design, the Gorged Condition is generally the time to start sowing the seeds of your larger scale ambitions, and Nightmares are good for that.<br /> 2) Dragons are one of the more notional cryptids to build on, so you can justify almost anything in terms of Atavism, so it pays to consider what specific idea of a dragon you're going for. I could justify the majority of most Family's Atavisms except for the Inguma for dragons.<br /> 3) I don't recall particular rules for this, so I would wager that armor from merits and Unbreakable can stack. Contrawise, I don't think mundane armor and mystical sources of armor stack, but ask me again when I'm not having breakfast.<br /> 4) Those are good merits, yep. Your character's definitely setting up to be the Hitter.<br /> 5) You might ask your Storyteller about setting expectations and pick a Minor Lair trait that they would agree is likely to come up. It sounds good, but it wouldn't be good if the story is mostly set, say, on a cross country hike through wilds.<br /> 6) So while you are setup to be a primary fighter for the group, you might want to consider what your soft second role is going to be, particular with party comp in mind. As mentioned as well, you probably want to focus more on what you want your legend (not not Legend but also not Legend) to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T21:17:03-08:00","id":1504103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Variable</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1504048-complete-beast-newb-creation-help#post1504048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Does the armor from Unbreakable stack with Advanced Ironskin or just normally wearing body armor (or anything else)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Says it right in the last line before the Dice Pool: &quot;Armor from this Atavism is cumulative with mundane sources of armor and the Iron Skin Merit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}